From: appkins <nbatkins@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 31 Aug 2026 10:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] PlatformBm: connect the onboard NIC before the Redfish sync

RpiRedfishSyncDxe reports the host's Ethernet interfaces from the SNP
handles that already exist - its exchange runs at TPL_CALLBACK, where
ConnectController is not permitted, so it cannot connect anything
itself. On a disk boot nothing else connects the RP1 GEM, and the NIC
inventory only ever populated on boots that happened to netboot.

Connect the network device class in PlatformBootManagerAfterConsole,
right before the USB NIC gate opens. BootManagerPolicyDxe connects the
device paths cached in its non-volatile network list and only falls
back to a full ConnectAll when that cache is empty, so warm boots pay
for connecting the GEM alone; the still-closed USB NIC gate keeps the
RHI out of both the fallback connect and the cached list. This also
lets a Pxe or Usb boot override match on its first pass instead of its
connect-and-retry pass.
---

diff --git a/Platform/RaspberryPi/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBm.c b/Platform/RaspberryPi/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBm.c
index 3664c09..6ed3a5a 100644
--- a/Platform/RaspberryPi/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBm.c
+++ b/Platform/RaspberryPi/Library/PlatformBootManagerLib/PlatformBm.c
@@ -1006,6 +1006,49 @@ WaitForRedfishSyncSettled (
     __func__, RPI_SYNC_WAIT_POLLS * 100));
 }
 
+/**
+  Connect the onboard NIC so the Redfish sync can inventory it.
+
+  RpiRedfishSyncDxe reports the host's Ethernet interfaces to the BMC from
+  the SNP handles that already exist, and its exchange runs from
+  TPL_CALLBACK, where ConnectController is not permitted - it cannot
+  connect anything itself. On a disk boot nothing else connects the RP1
+  GEM, so without this call the NIC inventory only ever populated on boots
+  that happened to netboot. Connecting here also lets a Pxe or Usb boot
+  override match on its first pass instead of its connect-and-retry pass.
+
+  ConnectDeviceClass(Network) connects the device paths cached in
+  BootManagerPolicyDxe's non-volatile network list; only when that cache
+  is empty (first boot, or hardware changed) does it fall back to a full
+  ConnectAll to rebuild it. The USB NIC gate is still closed at this
+  point, so NetworkCommon never binds the RHI during that fallback and
+  the BMC's gadget NIC stays out of the cached list.
+**/
+STATIC
+VOID
+ConnectOnboardNicForInventory (
+  VOID
+  )
+{
+  EFI_STATUS                        Status;
+  EFI_BOOT_MANAGER_POLICY_PROTOCOL  *Policy;
+
+  Status = gBS->LocateProtocol (
+                  &gEfiBootManagerPolicyProtocolGuid,
+                  NULL,
+                  (VOID **)&Policy
+                  );
+  if (EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
+    return;
+  }
+
+  Status = Policy->ConnectDeviceClass (
+                     Policy,
+                     &gEfiBootManagerPolicyNetworkGuid
+                     );
+  DEBUG ((DEBUG_INFO, "%a: network class connect - %r\n", __func__, Status));
+}
+
 /**
   Do the platform specific action after the console is ready
   Possible things that can be done in PlatformBootManagerAfterConsole:
@@ -1060,6 +1103,8 @@ PlatformBootManagerAfterConsole (
 
   PlatformRegisterOptionsAndKeys ();
 
+  ConnectOnboardNicForInventory ();
+
   if (ConnectUsbNicDevices ()) {
     WaitForRedfishSyncSettled ();
   }
